 a 1564 shrine gong inscription, but a letter of Imagawa Yoshimoto published in 2009 mentions \"Nishio Castle\" and is dated to the Kira revolt of 1555 — now the earliest record.","刈谷市":"First recorded as \"Kariya township\" (借屋郷) in 1409; Sengoku-era sources write 苅屋 or かり屋, and the 刈谷 spelling came later.","小牧市":"From the pre-merger town of Komaki. One story: the sea once reached Mount Komaki, and sailors furled their sails (ho-maki) on sighting it; another: a medieval horse market — \"koma-ki\", horses coming.","瀬戸市":"\"Seto\" originally meant the spot where a narrow, fast stream opens out — as the valley does here. Another theory derives it from \"sueto\", a pottery place.","あま市":"The three towns belonged to Ama (海部) District, and the city took that name in hiragana. \"Nishi-Nagoya\", \"Meisei\" and \"Kaitō\" were also on the list before the merger council chose \"Ama\".","犬山市":"Three theories: good hunting with dogs (inu); a corruption of \"Ono-yama\" from Ono township; or \"inui-yama\", the hill to the northwest (inui) of Ōagata Shrine. 犬山 appears as early as the Nanzan junshu-roku of 1336.","知立市":"Wooden tags of the late 7th century write \"Chirifu\" (知利布), those of the 8th \"知立\". As a Tōkaidō post town it was written 池鯉鮒 — \"pond of carp and crucian\" — after the fish in the shrine pond.","清須市":"An old name: the 14th-century Jinpōshō lists the \"Kiyosu estate\". Two spellings coexist — 清須 in the Mikawa Monogatari, 清洲 in the Shinchō Kōki — with older texts favouring 清須.","豊明市":"Said to combine Toyokura, a sake brewery near today's Zengo Station from the early 1800s, with \"Meiji\"; the town history instead cites the palace harvest banquet Toyo-no-akari no sechie.","みよし市":"Said to be named after Miyoshi near Hōrai-ji, home of the monk Gyōkan; the spelling 三好 dates from the Kanbun era (1661–1673).","愛西市":"In the west (sai) of Aichi (ai). None of ten candidates won a majority, so Aisai beat Kaisei in a run-off.","田原市":"Kumano mountain ascetics who arrived in the mid-Heian period named the settlement after a place in Kii — today's Kushimoto, Wakayama. Nearby Mount Zaō has the same origin."}},"kyu":{"23101":{"t":8,"k":7864,"r":[["Owari Domain",7864]]},"23102":{"t":1,"k":541,"r":[["Owari Domain",541]]},"23103":{"t":19,"k":18229,"r":[["Owari Domain",14507],["Imao Domain",2835],["Inuyama Domain",887]]},"23104":{"t":12,"k":20777,"r":[["Owari Domain",18729],["Imao Domain",1400],["@hatamoto",348],["@jisha",300]]},"23105":{"t":12,"k":15614,"r":[["Owari Domain",15614]]},"23106":{"t":3,"k":5615,"r":[["Owari Domain",5615]]},"23107":{"t":6,"k":12788,"r":[["Owari Domain",12231],["Inuyama Domain",513],["@jisha",44]]},"23108":{"t":8,"k":6337,"r":[["Owari Domain",6335],["@jisha",2]]},"23109":{"t":4,"k":6421,"r":[["@jisha",4651],["Owari Domain",1769],["@other",1]]},"23110":{"t":48,"k":34938,"r":[["Owari Domain",32832],["Inuyama Domain",901],["Imao Domain",779],["@jisha",427]]},"23111":{"t":12,"k":8368,"r":[["Owari Domain",8285],["@jisha",82],["@other",1]]},"23112":{"t":15,"k":9059,"r":[["Owari Domain",8308],["Imao Domain",651],["@jisha",100]]},"23113":{"t":14,"k":9950,"r":[["Owari Domain",9726],["Inuyama Domain",219],["@jisha",5]]},"23114":{"t":6,"k":4997,"r":[["Owari Domain",4997]]},"23115":{"t":4,"k":2131,"r":[["Owari Domain",2131]]},"23116":{"t":4,"k":3358,"r":[["Owari Domain",1724],["@jisha",1634]]},"23201":{"t":129,"k":52658,"r":[["Yoshida Domain",43086],["@bakufu",4143],["@hatamoto",2166],["Okabe Domain",2062],["@other",1201]]},"23202":{"t":251,"k":71724,"r":[["Okazaki Domain",44073],["@hatamoto",11723],["@jisha",4866],["Nishi-Ōhira Domain",2588],["@other",8474]]},"23203":{"t":129,"k":84152,"r":[["Owari Domain",81435],["Imao Domain",1387],["Inuyama Domain",946],["@jisha",229],["@other",155]]},"23204":{"t":18,"k":8941,"r":[["Owari Domain",8941]]},"23205":{"t":6,"k":9956,"r":[["Inuyama Domain",6112],["Owari Domain",3786],["@jisha",58]]},"23206":{"t":52,"k":25909,"r":[["Owari Domain",24529],["Inuyama Domain",1184],["@jisha",172],["Imao 